HST Office: gtk3 windows with a native menu bar report the screen position of their content, so accessible objects are no longer 27 px too high.

On Linux (gtk3) every VCL accessible object of a window that shows the native GTK menu bar was reported one menu bar
height (27 px) above where it is drawn: AT-SPI gave the Start Center's root pane y 25 while the GTK container that
holds it starts at y 52 (LibreOffice 26.8.3.1 and HST 1.0.2/1.0.3 alike; documents under the Tabbed UI have no menu
bar and were right). Orca's flat review, magnifiers following focus and AT-SPI test drivers point above the object.

Cause: the frame geometry (SalFrameGeometry) is that of the VCL content, the event box below the menu bar: its size
is the drawing area's, and UpdateGeometryFromEvent takes the position from mouse events relative to the event box.
signalConfigure, however, stored the toplevel's position from the configure event, which is above the content by
the menu bar. vcl::Window::OutputToAbsoluteScreenPixel adds that position, so accessible extents
(VCLXAccessibleComponent::getLocationOnScreen), VCL popups positioned in absolute coordinates and SetPointerPos
were off by the menu bar until the next mouse event over the window corrected the position; a keyboard-only user
never sends one. The menu bar is also built on an idle after the window shows (hst-gtk-menubar-lazy-build), and shown
or hidden later (.uno:Menubar, full screen), which moves the content without a configure event.

GtkSalFrame now adds the content's offset inside the toplevel (gtk_widget_translate_coordinates of the event box to
the GtkWindow; 0 without a menu bar) to the configure position, counts the menu bar into the top decoration (so
position minus top decoration is still the window frame's top: GetWindowExtentsAbsolute, embedded frames), and
updates position and decoration when the drawing area is allocated with a new offset. SetScreen subtracts the
offset again before gtk_window_move, which places the toplevel. Window state still uses gtk_window_get_position, so
saved and restored window positions do not change. Wayland: the configure position is 0 and the same offset is what
mouse events already gave.

Hook: vcl/unx/gtk3/gtkframe.cxx (signalConfigure, DrawingAreaResized, SetScreen, two helpers),
vcl/inc/unx/gtk/gtkframe.hxx (two members, two declarations).
Test: tests/runtime/check-gtk3-a11y-offset.py (AT-SPI: root pane y equals its GTK container's y and starts below a
showing menu bar, on the Start Center and on a Writer document whose menu bar is switched on and off).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
